From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Tue, 06 Oct 2026 19:41:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: skip unbound links in a chanctx switch

A driver can leave a link without a channel context while its
firmware has no state for the link, for example after a full reset.
A channel switch that ran before mac80211 restored the link bound it
to the new context anyway, so beacon and BSS updates reached the
firmware before the BSS existed.

A link without a context now stays unbound in a switch, and the phy
still moves to the new channel. mac80211 assigns the link again when
it restores the hardware.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 channel.c |    5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/channel.c
+++ b/channel.c
@@ -254,8 +254,11 @@ int mt76_switch_vif_chanctx(struct ieee8
 			need_update[phy->band_idx] = false;
 		}
 
+		/* a link without a context is not set up in the driver, for
+		 * example after a full reset; mac80211 assigns it again later
+		 */
 		mlink = mt76_vif_conf_link(dev, v->vif, v->link_conf);
-		if (!mlink)
+		if (!mlink || !mlink->ctx)
 			continue;
 
 		if (old_phy != phy) {
